            <ArticleTitle>Intercoronary communication in chronic total occlusion: In search of recognition.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>S90-S92</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0019-4832(16)30261-9</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.ihj.2016.07.005</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Intercoronary communications (ICC) or open-ended coronary circulation is rare. We describe intercoronary communication in a case of chronic total occlusion, and discuss the pathophysiological and clinical significance of these rare entities. The present case also demonstrates the anatomical presence of ICC despite angiographic absence for the first time using CT coronary angiography.</AbstractText>
